187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (The cracking and apparent instability of the heavier plaster sections above the entry door are of particular concern. Based on their location, thickness and observed cracking, these sections should be considered a potential falling-object hazard and should be professionally assessed and made secure. If a section were to detach and fall onto a person, the potential for significant injury exists.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
188 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (The extensive bubbling and peeling of external paint is consistent with moisture being present beneath the coating. In the climate of Bali, continued moisture exposure can contribute to deterioration of masonry and render and can provide conditions conducive to mould and mildew growth. The presence of visible mould at this stage is of particular concern given the substantially greater moisture exposure expected during the wet season.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (The exposed electrical wiring represents a potential electrical safety hazard, particularly given the property's exposure to humidity, rain and external environmental conditions. The wiring should be appropriately enclosed, protected and assessed by a suitably qualified electrical professional.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
