327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (Throughout the residence, there are repeated indications of poor workmanship, inadequate finishing, moisture penetration, cracking masonry and plasterwork, insufficient ventilation, mould and mildew development, and deficiencies in building services. In addition, the property water system, tested from the kitchen supply, has been professionally tested and recorded, the tenants will supply the relevant certificates and reports along with this construction and safety report. However, the test results are a concern for occupants using this water for showering, bathing and personal hygiene.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (Several conditions identified also have potential physical safety implications, including inadequately bonded and heavily cracked plaster above doorways, deteriorated pool coping grout, cloudy pool water, exposed electrical wiring, concerns regarding the gas installation, and reported electrical failures. While not every observed defect represents an immediate danger, the cumulative condition of the property presents a level of risk that warrants serious consideration.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (The absence of adequate natural or mechanical ventilation in the enclosed bedrooms is particularly concerning when considered together with the existing moisture damage, mould growth and substantial heat accumulation. In Bali's climate, these conditions can become significantly more difficult to control during the wet season, when increased rainfall and humidity provide more favourable conditions for moisture retention and mould and mildew development.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
